# Terraform
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Plan and state output holds every credential in cleartext.
#
# `terraform show -json <planfile>` emits a `variables` block containing the
# value of every input variable - the Arc service-principal secret, the Proxmox
# API token, the Proxmox root SSH password and both guest admin passwords.
# `sensitive = true` marks CLI output, not the JSON representation, so it
# redacts nothing here, and the block is populated even when the plan changes
# nothing at all.
#
# State output carries a different but equally sensitive payload: the rendered
# cloud-init snippet in `source_raw.data`, which embeds the same credentials.
#
# Verified 2026-08-22 against a real build artifact. See issue #34 (SEC-002).
tfplan
tfplan.json
tfstate.json
arc_delete_names.txt

# Variable files
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!example.tfvars

# Claude Code
# settings.local.json is per-machine and never shared. settings.json *can* be
# committed to share a permission allowlist with a team - delete the second
# line below if you ever want that. Today it holds only one-off permissions
# accumulated during a working session, which are not worth sharing.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.json

# Editor / OS
# .vscode/* rather than .vscode/: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a `!` negation below cannot re-include anything unless the
# directory itself stays walkable. Two files are shared on purpose and the rest
# of the directory stays local. settings.json formats .tf on save;
# extensions.json recommends the extension that setting names as its formatter,
# which is inert without it. Both are conveniences - the fmt gate is the
# terraform job in checks.yml, which does not depend on anyone's editor.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Python
# The scripts in .github/scripts are run as `python3 <file>`, but the test
# suites import two of them, and an import writes bytecode next to the source.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
